# Accepted risks. EVERY entry needs a written reason. Run `local-setup/scan.sh trivy-fs` and keep this list as short as possible.
# Format: one finding ID per line; comments above it.

# --- Terraform: CloudFront / ALB design (see README "Decisions & trade-offs") ---------------------------------------
# ALB is internet-facing by design: its security group only accepts CloudFront origin-facing IPs and the listener
# forwards only requests with the secret X-Origin-Verify header (VPC origins make it internal: stretch goal).
AWS-0053
# CloudFront -> ALB is plain HTTP in this lab (needs a custom domain + ACM certificate: stretch goal). Traffic stays
# inside AWS and is protected by the header secret + CloudFront-only security group.
AWS-0054
# No AWS WAF in front of CloudFront: cost (WAF ~ 6+ USD/month) and out of scope for the lab.
AWS-0011
# CloudFront default certificate (*.cloudfront.net) cannot enforce TLS >= 1.2; fixed with a custom domain (stretch goal).
AWS-0012
# --- Terraform: EKS public API endpoint -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GitHub-hosted runners (Helm provider) and the student laptop reach the API over the internet. Access is IAM-only
# (access entries); a private endpoint + self-hosted runner is the production setup.
AWS-0040
AWS-0041
# --- Terraform: IAM wildcards ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ecr:GetAuthorizationToken and Describe* read-only calls only exist with Resource "*".
AWS-0057
